                   stop subsequent actions in the enclosing entry/exit
                   block (W3C 5.10). Mirrors cpp `ForeachHelper.h:158-195`
                   `evaluateForeachArray` returning nullopt → caller raise.
                   The `return;` terminates only the surrounding entry/exit
